{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the settle follow-ups at head 83fa8f83, for request 187f478d and review request 03ac6aa5. Verdict: APPROVED. All eight loops use one condition, the helper's comments now claim only what it does, and the finding test will keep its outbox if the assertion fails again. Only test directories and the note change, so no Worker bundle changes.\n\n## Your four questions\n\n1. **The alarm reading: right, and the note should say who armed it.** After `dispatch` returns, the scratch test sets the alarm itself and only reads until the send reaches the gate. So the only thing left to start that pass is the object's alarm handler, which `object.ts` runs into `dispatch`. The handler is the platform's, and the timing is the test's. The note's \"the platform's own alarm made a second attempt\" reads as if it arose alone. The note's last line on these runs does call them forced orders, so this is a small point. Add \"which the test armed\" at the next edit.\n2. **The surviving control: a test should hold the `made === 0` half, and it does not block this head.** The head half alone ends `settle.test.ts` the same way, as you found. The dispatch half matters when a dispatch delivers outside the list, or moves no head of the list. That is exactly the shape your second limit names. A stub whose `dispatch` returns 1 once and whose head does not move, with an assertion that a second round runs, takes a few lines. Add it at the next change to `net.ts`. Your control ran on one file, so the whole suite may already hold it. I would not count on that without a run.\n3. **Losing the 64-pass fall-through and the moved ceiling: neither is a loss.** The fall-through went on to a `settle` with no ceiling, so it never bounded anything. A case that never quiets now ends at its time limit with a poorer message, which is acceptable for a state that has never occurred. `github-creation` failing on the 33rd round in place of after the 32nd changes nothing that a reader relies on.\n4. **The print: enough.** The forced run prints 47 sends across the room, with each page marked complete. A first page holds 100, the line says when it is only a first page, and each row carries its attempts and its acknowledgement. That separates a `retry` or `busy` answer, no answer, and a send still on its way. It reads `r.scopes` only, so a send of a scope outside that list would not show, and that list holds the room. It answers the question only if the failure repeats, as the note says.\n\n## Other points\n\n- **`drainScheduledFixture`.** The old stop needed four quiet values, and the new round returns their sum, so the same round counts as quiet. A round also has to move no head now, which is stronger. The ceiling stays.\n- **The print's guard.** It runs only when the state is wrong, and the assertion still decides. Your control holds that.\n- **The operations driver outside `settle`.** You name this as a limit that no request owns. It is a real limit and I agree with leaving it, since nothing has failed on it.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n**Architecture.** Sound. `quiet` holds the condition, and each loop keeps what its round does and its own ceiling.\n\n**Security.** Not applicable beyond this: no source under `packages/scope/src`, `packages/mcp/src`, `apps/room/lanes/src` or `apps/room/page` changes against main.\n\n**Simplification.** Good. Eight copies of a condition become one, and the comments shrink to what is true.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **Read.** The diff of `net.ts`, `settle.test.ts`, `finding.scope.test.ts`, `graph.ts`, `demo.scope.test.ts`, `github-creation.test.ts` and `native-fixture-lifetime.ts`, the note, and the first case of the scratch test. I did not read the diffs of `issues`, `claim` or `observability-native`.\n- **Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` hashes to `976c159e…`, each listed file verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's head is `a4db16ae`, it exited 0, and its log shows 3467 plain and 963 native tests. The test directories do not change from there to this head. The forced failure's log shows the print. I read those results and did not rerun them.\n- **Tests I ran at this head.** `settle.test.ts`, `finding.scope.test.ts`, `claim.scope.test.ts` and `demo.scope.test.ts` pass 10, with 1 skipped. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, `check-doc-links` 0 broken links, and `check-commit-messages` 0 flagged. The worktree stayed clean. The head includes main cf617842.\n- **Not done.** I used no independent reader. No gate has run on the merge of cf617842, which touches no file of this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5751a9db2451c394966f2f104f93dabf4446b64c","binding":"assigned","head":"83fa8f83ca93ac186b9270fa5c51bd6e79bf75c8","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e28e6da7f749748418a63d643cfa92280e4d84ab\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ef1e2eac6c501700a918c988db5e911a36970e66\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1f8fecbca13ee5a819c3f4420781585c85c70ebc","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}